Z||000000||fierobaby||06-16-2001||12:15 PM||||Ok all my Fiero's driver seat is frozen.  I can move the little lever under the seat and nothing happens.  The seat wont move.  can someone tell me how to get the seat to move?  Or get it moved to get the seat out of the car so i can replace the seat braket. <P>Thanks<BR>Fierobaby<BR>(Corinne)<P>84' coupe<BR>Sweet Candy apple red||||reg||3
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||06-16-2001||12:24 PM||||That must be COLD!<BR>Try soaking the racks (where you can get to them) with some penatrating oil and let set for a while. If they still won't move you will need to use an open end 13mm wrench to remove the nuts. The front ones will be the easiest but the back ones will be a bear!||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||06-16-2001||01:24 PM||||Also make sure the wire that controls the lock mechanism isn't broken. If you can move the lever and the mechanism moves then it's probably just seized to the track.<P>Welcome to the group!<P>Gary<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||kslish||06-16-2001||04:41 PM||||Judging by the pictures and description of your car in the other thread I'll assume the seat rails aren't rusted solid... It sounds like the lever wire that FieroBUZZ mentions is broken...it connects the lever to the seat rail opposite to one the lever is directly connected to.  What is probably happening is that one seat rail is releasing (the one the lever is attached to) but the other side is remaining locked because of the connecting wire being broke.<P>It may be possible to squeeze a hand under there to manually actuate the other seat rail...if you can get the front seat rail floor bolts out with an open end wrench you should be able to tilt the seat back some to give more room to work.  <P>It may also be helpful to pull the passenger seat out of the car (It's like a 5-10 minute job at best) so you can look at the seat rail mechanism to familiarize yourself with how everything works and moves.  That way you'll know what you need to grab ahold of to release the stubborn one on the driver's side.<P><P>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A>||||reg||1
